Repo gates also green at this commit: make test, make lint.

muserisc_mmu (408 lines): one unified 32-entry fully-associative
TLB with fetch and data combinational lookup ports, one walker
sharing the core data port (data misses preempt fetch walks;
MEM keeps the port whenever it has a usable access), Sv39
4K/2M/1G leaves, Svnapot 64K, ASID+global matching, hardware
A/D updates (Svadu semantics, store hit with D=0 re-walks and
overwrites the same TLB slot), full-flush SFENCE.VMA, and a
recorded-fault protocol that cannot negative-cache (a fault
dies when its port's VA moves on). PMP applies to translated
PAs; a third PMP port checks implicit PTE accesses as S-mode,
and PMP denial of an A/D writeback surfaces as an access
fault. satp MODE is WARL-clamped to Bare/Sv39 in the CSR file.

mmu_tb.cpp drives the module against a TB memory holding
hand-built tables: Bare/M passthrough, walks at all levels,
both superpages (incl. misaligned), NAPOT, canonicality,
malformed PTEs (W-without-R, reserved bits, bad N, pointer at
L0, non-leaf A/D/U), U/SUM/MXR rules, A/D memory writebacks,
ASID/global/flush, port-denial and grant-stall behavior, the
A/D-writeback PMP denial, fault auto-clear, and data
preemption of a fetch walk. vm_directed.S then runs 14 groups
on the core: translated loads/stores/execute, page faults
12/13/15 with tval checks, MXR, SUM, a U-mode excursion from
a U-page stub, A/D updates observed in memory, SFENCE
staleness, NAPOT, a 2M superpage with a 4K alias, and MPRV.
Three bugs found while bringing the test up were all in the
test itself (U stub initially linked into a U=0 page, the
S handler consuming an M-intended redirect cell for a U trap,
and a misaligned sd); the RTL needed no functional fixes,
only expression-form rewrites of two TLB helper functions
whose early returns Verilator coverage cannot attribute.
